<title>CHILE: Codelco's El Teniente copper pit signs wage deal.</title>
<headline>Codelco's El Teniente copper pit signs wage deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>El Teniente, the second largest of state copper company Codelco's four mines, has signed a four year labor contract with pit supervisors, said the division.</p>
<p>The deal will be in force for 48 months from October 1, said the statement.</p>
<p>The pact includes an increase in salaries as well as a rise in profit-related bonuses, it said.</p>
<p>El Teniente, which lies south of Santiago, produced 322,843 tonnes of fine copper last year.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
</text>
